  "version": 1,
  "title": "Generic IP-transitive points in weakly mixing systems",
  "abstract": "For a continuous map of a second-countable Baire Hausdorff space with topologically transitive square, a residual set of points has IP entering times into every nonempty open set. A nonempty space has a nonempty dense G-delta family of such points; square hitting times are infinite.",
